GPL-2.0-or-later; UDS and Download Play logic derives from Azahar/Citra.
Bundled ENet core: MIT, licence in enet/LICENSE.

Imported subset:
- UDS engine, frame codec, crypto and room packet codec.
- Room client, platform/logging support and dependency headers.
- Download Play hub, lobby network, real network/wire and the C dlph_wire codec.
- ENet core and its platform headers.

Wii U adaptations:
- Explicit guest little-endian ConnectionStatus serialization and numeric IPC
  conversion for UTF-16 names, node records and nine-byte reboot passphrases.
- Integer conversion of host/PPC ticks to the ARM11 protocol clock.
- enet/wiiu.c, derived from upstream unix.c, uses sendto/recvfrom in place of
  unavailable scatter/gather calls. Both receive-buffer address and requested
  capacity are 64-byte aligned. Nonblocking receives use MSG_DONTWAIT.
- The runtime bridge stamps outgoing frames with the room-assigned MAC and
  maps service events to guest handles. DLP adapters currently select Mario Kart
  title IDs; transport configuration is shared across all rebuilt games.

Checks and limitations:
- Upstream uds_eight_test under host ASan/UBSan passed 15,798 checks, including
  two acknowledged upstream gaps. dlp_ipc_test against the adapted headers passed
  827,897 checks in the local investigation.
- Local UDP adapter checks cover nonblocking reads, scatter/gather, truncation,
  oversized writes and native receive alignment.
- Real Wii U room connection, Tri Force Heroes Cemu/Azahar lobby join, and Mario
  Kart Cemu/locally patched Azahar lobby/race startup have been observed. These
  do not establish all-game compatibility or complete hardware gameplay.
- Current configuration and verification limits are documented in
  tools/wiiu_diagnostics/TRIFORCE_MULTIPLAYER_STATUS.md.
